WEBVTT

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:04.290
Raetsel...

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:09.710
That’s right. I’m Raetsel, Jin.

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:13.210
The annihilation of all puzzlers...

00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:15.760
in accordance with a pledge 
I swore to Jin Makata.

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:21.880
If you can’t solve my puzzle, just 
like you’re buddies, you’re...!

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:28.920
I’m going to defeat you with a puzzle.

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:32.600
I’m using the thing Jin hated 
and detested above all else,

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:36.010
wishing that they’d fall of 
the face of the planet: Puzzles!

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:10.980
You Don’t Know Anything

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:22.320
We’ve gotta find the right door fast

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:24.300
and make a break for it or else...!

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:25.270
Kaito...

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:33.000
Say, Jin?

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:37.010
Jin, didn’t you hate rats?

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:38.810
But you know,

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:41.010
I love them!

00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:48.520
The statue rotates each 
time she snaps her fingers.

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:51.660
That’s our only key 
to solving this puzzle.

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:54.150
What does it mean...?

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:56.440
That’s it!

00:02:57.250 --> 00:02:59.480
There is no way the 
correct door would move

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:01.690
if the statue was simply rotating!

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:04.780
But it did move.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.020
Which means...!

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:09.290
Kaito!

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:14.060
That statue hasn’t rotated 
once this whole time!

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:14.730
What?

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:18.440
It was the room that was rotating!

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:20.400
Each time she snapped,

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:23.340
the correct door moved away 
from the starting point.

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:27.490
Raetsel has snapped her 
fingers six times so far!

00:03:27.490 --> 00:03:30.810
So right now, the one 
connected to the exit is...

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:32.560
this door!

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:34.950
What?!

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:36.000
A dead end?!

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:39.650
Too bad! You’re wrong.

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:41.530
Look out, Kaito!

00:03:57.220 --> 00:04:01.020
I’m the Master Brain, Whodunit.

00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:04.440
I’d like to begin with 
a super-important warning.

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:06.650
Go ahead and try to escape!

00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:10.360
You’ll never get to 
solve puzzles ever again!

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:14.060
What?! Don’t talk in riddles!

00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:18.570
The demon will devour you!

00:04:19.330 --> 00:04:22.260
You’ve made it crystal 
clear just how messed up

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:23.380
you are in the head.

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:26.160
I accept your challenge!

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:30.160
I’ll put everything I’ve 
got into crushing you!

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:38.060
Rook!

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:39.420
Rook!

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:42.350
I’m fine...

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:43.770
It just grazed me.

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:45.930
Raetsel!

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:49.940
The next one is your last chance!

00:04:50.150 --> 00:04:53.160
You really will die if you get it wrong.

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:56.100
What’s going on?

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:59.830
She made it look like the statue 
was rotating instead of the room.

00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:02.080
That was supposed to be 
the key to this puzzle!

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:06.790
Am I overlooking something?

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:12.800
If you can’t solve a 
low-level puzzle like this,

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:16.260
did you fail to learn anything from Jin?

00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:17.210
From Jin?

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:21.210
What I’ve learned from Jin...

00:05:21.850 --> 00:05:22.810
That’s...

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:27.310
Kaito, solve them. Set them free.

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:28.470
Free the puzzles.

00:05:29.230 --> 00:05:31.470
I’ll solve any puzzle I come across!

00:05:36.030 --> 00:05:39.480
There's no puzzle I can't solve!

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:48.590
I’m confident that 
the room was rotating.

00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:51.510
But so was the statue!

00:05:52.090 --> 00:05:56.980
She differentiated the two 
with her right and left hands.

00:05:57.390 --> 00:06:00.720
Based on that, there are five 
potentially correct answers.

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:10.580
The questions are: How many times

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:12.860
did Raetsel snap her 
fingers on each hand?

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:17.100
And which hand correlates 
with the room and

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:18.490
which with the statue?

00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:19.330
Kaito!

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:22.650
I remember the number of snaps.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:26.810
She snapped three times on 
both her right and left hands.

00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:33.370
Let’s go, Rook! Nonoha!

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:34.200
Yeah!

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:38.550
Both the room and statue have 
rotated three times each.

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:41.880
So right now, the correct exit is...

00:06:44.810 --> 00:06:45.720
I see.

00:06:47.310 --> 00:06:48.720
This puzzle...

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:52.850
This is the door!

00:06:55.820 --> 00:06:57.020
Bingo!

00:07:16.170 --> 00:07:17.030
Rook?

00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:20.080
Are you okay, Rook?

00:07:20.890 --> 00:07:21.820
Yeah!

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:26.890
I knew you’d remember!

00:07:26.890 --> 00:07:29.380
We made that puzzle together.

00:07:31.230 --> 00:07:32.970
I had a feeling...

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:35.570
I made that puzzle...

00:07:36.030 --> 00:07:37.130
What?!

00:07:38.530 --> 00:07:41.740
Hey, you! How do you and Jin--

00:07:41.740 --> 00:07:43.830
J-I-N!

00:07:44.450 --> 00:07:47.400
Jin remembered a piece of his past.

00:07:47.830 --> 00:07:50.790
No matter how hard you tried, 
you couldn’t jog his memories!

00:07:51.750 --> 00:07:57.550
Jin, you wished for all puzzlers 
in the world to be annihilated.

00:07:58.300 --> 00:08:00.340
I’ll make that dream come true, Jin.

00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:01.410
Cut the crap!

00:08:03.010 --> 00:08:05.130
Jin would never say something like that!

00:08:05.260 --> 00:08:09.180
What? Are you saying 
that Jin loved puzzles?

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:12.630
That’s right! Jin loved 
puzzles more than anyone.

00:08:13.190 --> 00:08:14.820
Yeah?

00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:21.070
Sure enough, you don’t 
know anything about Jin.

00:08:21.820 --> 00:08:22.430
Wha--?!

00:08:22.780 --> 00:08:24.780
Come on, Jin. Let’s go.

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:27.790
Wait! Hey! Where’re you going?!

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:29.440
Care to join us?

00:08:31.420 --> 00:08:34.540
I’ll tell you about the true Jin.

00:08:40.170 --> 00:08:43.900
Why does a mere girl have 
access to a private jet?

00:08:44.470 --> 00:08:45.960
It would seem that a

00:08:46.390 --> 00:08:48.830
powerful underground 
organization is backing her.

00:09:04.910 --> 00:09:07.560
What’s with this massive ship?!

00:09:20.630 --> 00:09:24.260
That is the Republic of 
Amgine’s coat of arms.

00:09:25.340 --> 00:09:29.680
So this ship belongs to 
the Republic of Amgine?

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:35.350
Relax. I can move around 
freely on this ship.

00:09:35.730 --> 00:09:37.690
My contract says so.

00:09:53.870 --> 00:09:56.110
Jin loved puzzles!

00:09:56.630 --> 00:09:58.730
That’s your assertion, right?

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:00.120
Yeah.

00:10:00.590 --> 00:10:02.240
This is the truth.

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:09.190
What the heck?

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:11.310
Who are all of these people?

00:10:12.350 --> 00:10:14.620
Puzzlers who have been defeated by

00:10:14.620 --> 00:10:17.220
Master Brains and will 
never play puzzles again.

00:10:17.770 --> 00:10:19.270
Master Brains...?

00:10:19.270 --> 00:10:22.190
Jin, he doesn’t know anything!

00:10:24.530 --> 00:10:28.990
Right now, Master Brains are 
hunting puzzlers around the world.

00:10:29.830 --> 00:10:32.490
All to realize Jin’s ideal world!

00:10:36.870 --> 00:10:38.080
The guys!

00:10:38.080 --> 00:10:40.000
What... are they...?

00:10:41.210 --> 00:10:43.190
We annihilate puzzlers

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:45.870
with their beloved puzzles.

00:10:46.470 --> 00:10:47.960
Isn’t that right, Jin?

00:10:51.220 --> 00:10:51.960
Just you watch.

00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:56.600
Behold the terror of the 
puzzles you despised.

00:11:04.530 --> 00:11:07.580
I have some good news for you!

00:11:08.030 --> 00:11:11.580
Apparently Kaito Daimon 
successfully freed a puzzle.

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:13.740
I figured.

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:14.160
Hurray!

00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:15.370
Ana!
 Hurray!

00:11:16.460 --> 00:11:21.110
Now for some BAD NEWS!

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:28.750
Crap! Run for it!

00:11:33.850 --> 00:11:34.780
What the--?

00:11:35.100 --> 00:11:36.270
Run!

00:11:41.940 --> 00:11:43.520
Ow, ow, ow...

00:11:51.570 --> 00:11:53.040
Iwashimizu!

00:11:56.080 --> 00:11:57.940
Jerk! What’s your game?

00:11:58.540 --> 00:12:02.030
Welcome to my puzzle!

00:12:02.540 --> 00:12:05.840
The cubes present will 
serve as your hint.

00:12:05.840 --> 00:12:09.660
Fill all of the holes on the 
puzzle board with cubes!

00:12:10.340 --> 00:12:13.270
The seven colors include: Red, blue,

00:12:13.270 --> 00:12:17.500
yellow, purple, orange, green and black!

00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:20.440
You have a ten-minute time limit.

00:12:20.440 --> 00:12:22.220
Once ten minutes pass,

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:26.250
I’ll send an electric current across 
the floor that’ll do this...

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:34.980
Shuddup, ya confused yapper!

00:12:35.910 --> 00:12:38.410
I can solve this puzzle by myself.

00:12:38.910 --> 00:12:40.360
Let the other two go free.

00:12:40.870 --> 00:12:42.700
Gammon Sakanoue!

00:12:43.880 --> 00:12:46.090
$750,000.

00:12:46.470 --> 00:12:47.200
You givin’ that to me?

00:12:47.800 --> 00:12:49.330
Cubik Galois!

00:12:49.550 --> 00:12:51.550
$650,000.

00:12:53.220 --> 00:12:54.350
Ana Gram!

00:12:54.350 --> 00:12:55.970
$900,000.

00:12:56.180 --> 00:12:56.930
Huh?

00:12:58.390 --> 00:13:01.090
Punk! What’re you goin’ on about?

00:13:01.390 --> 00:13:06.760
They’re the bounties placed 
on you Phi-Brain children.

00:13:07.020 --> 00:13:09.260
What?! I’m the lowest?

00:13:07.080 --> 00:13:10.890
What?! I’m the lowest?

00:13:09.610 --> 00:13:13.820
Yay! I, Ana, am the highest!

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:12.280
Gimme!

00:13:12.680 --> 00:13:15.270
Why am I lower than Ana?

00:13:13.820 --> 00:13:16.280
Number 1! Number 1! Number 1!

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:18.350
Together, you reach a 
total of $2,300,000.

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:21.650
According to my contract, that 
is how much Enigma will pay

00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:23.400
if I defeat you.

00:13:23.540 --> 00:13:28.280
For the record, Kaito Daimon 
has a $10,000,000 bounty!

00:13:28.630 --> 00:13:31.720
What?! $10,000,000?!

00:13:31.720 --> 00:13:34.790
That right? Talk about a juicy job.

00:13:35.840 --> 00:13:38.290
$10,000,000! $10,000,000!

00:13:38.470 --> 00:13:39.900
Goodness gracious.

00:13:39.900 --> 00:13:44.270
If possible, I had wanted to 
take down Kaito Daimon myself.

00:13:44.270 --> 00:13:46.560
Compared to $10,000,000,

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:52.060
I’m practically volunteering 
my time to kill you three.

00:13:52.610 --> 00:13:55.660
What was that?! Don’t be stupid!

00:13:56.120 --> 00:13:59.060
I swear that I’ll 
crush your sorry ass!

00:13:59.580 --> 00:14:03.870
I’ll prove that I’m worth 
a flipping $20,000,000!

00:14:03.870 --> 00:14:06.750
Hey, punk! Are you even listening?!

00:14:07.210 --> 00:14:10.750
Try to put up a decent fight, $750,000!

00:14:11.300 --> 00:14:16.340
Now then... Puzzle time, start!

00:14:22.060 --> 00:14:25.170
This puzzle is ruled by a color code.

00:14:25.560 --> 00:14:28.480
Once I decipher that code, 
victory is as good as mine!

00:14:31.820 --> 00:14:33.890
Is this a...

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:36.270
number game with colors?!

00:14:37.490 --> 00:14:41.450
If that’s the case, there are over 
26 million possible combinations.

00:14:41.700 --> 00:14:44.580
I’ll never solve that in ten minutes!

00:14:44.870 --> 00:14:47.570
Just what I’d expect of $750,000.

00:14:47.880 --> 00:14:50.030
Declaring defeat already?

00:14:50.590 --> 00:14:53.380
Shuddup, ya confused yapper!

00:14:54.090 --> 00:14:57.550
Damn it! How the hell am 
I supposed to solve this?

00:15:00.850 --> 00:15:02.510
This is incredibly difficult...

00:15:03.390 --> 00:15:06.060
I cannot find so much as a hint or clue.

00:15:07.310 --> 00:15:08.300
Guys...

00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:11.470
Jin, watch careful.

00:15:12.110 --> 00:15:13.490
And then remember.

00:15:13.900 --> 00:15:16.200
Dredge up your hatred for puzzles.

00:15:18.070 --> 00:15:21.800
C’mon, hurry! $650,000 and $900,000,

00:15:21.800 --> 00:15:23.730
why don’t you help him out?

00:15:24.040 --> 00:15:27.710
Honestly, even if the three 
of you worked together,

00:15:28.040 --> 00:15:32.070
you couldn’t solve a puzzle 
created by this Master Brain!

00:15:32.550 --> 00:15:35.910
Jeez! What is a Master Brain anyway?!

00:15:37.010 --> 00:15:39.330
Those who made a pledge to Jin Makata

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:41.670
and surpass the Phi-Brain!

00:15:43.760 --> 00:15:46.480
Sheeit! There’s Jin 
Makata’s name again!

00:15:46.480 --> 00:15:49.400
In his hatred for puzzles and puzzlers,

00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:51.640
he wanted to eliminate 
the Phi-Brain children

00:15:51.640 --> 00:15:54.580
since you serve as their figureheads.

00:15:55.530 --> 00:15:58.430
That was Jin Makata’s logic.

00:15:58.570 --> 00:15:59.550
See?

00:16:05.200 --> 00:16:07.830
Gammon, we’re in trouble if 
you don’t make a breakthrough.

00:16:07.830 --> 00:16:09.960
I know that!

00:16:10.370 --> 00:16:13.210
Q-taro, what do you make of this puzzle?

00:16:15.750 --> 00:16:19.490
I stink at artsy puzzles like this.

00:16:20.260 --> 00:16:21.960
Oh, yeah! How about Ana?

00:16:22.600 --> 00:16:23.550
Huh?

00:16:24.560 --> 00:16:25.970
Ana!

00:16:27.140 --> 00:16:28.890
I, Ana, think...

00:16:30.100 --> 00:16:32.510
that I like this box the best!

00:16:34.520 --> 00:16:35.510
He’s no help...

00:16:35.770 --> 00:16:39.890
Oh, ouch! Done already, $750,000?

00:16:39.990 --> 00:16:42.870
Jerk! Quit callin’ me by my bounty!

00:16:42.870 --> 00:16:44.300
In three minutes,

00:16:44.300 --> 00:16:48.740
a toasty $2,300,000 
will fall into my lap!

00:16:49.790 --> 00:16:50.750
Shuddup!

00:16:50.750 --> 00:16:52.960
You’re toast! Toast!

00:16:51.170 --> 00:16:56.240
I’ll make you drop that freakin’ 
annoying laugh in three minutes!

00:16:59.260 --> 00:17:03.430
Go ahead and try, $750,000!

00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:08.180
These colors must mean something.

00:17:08.850 --> 00:17:10.810
If only I knew what...

00:17:11.270 --> 00:17:12.800
I, Ana, figured it out!

00:17:12.270 --> 00:17:12.800
What?!

00:17:13.400 --> 00:17:14.900
“Aka” is “red.”

00:17:19.490 --> 00:17:20.940
Dumbass!

00:17:20.940 --> 00:17:23.350
What’re you talkin’ about when 
I’m busy tryin’ to think?!

00:17:23.740 --> 00:17:28.660
Wait! Isn’t he saying that we 
should spell the colors in English?

00:17:31.870 --> 00:17:33.210
“Aka” is “red.”

00:17:33.210 --> 00:17:34.830
“Kiiro” is “yellow.”

00:17:34.830 --> 00:17:36.430
If you consider how many 
letters is in each

00:17:36.430 --> 00:17:37.790
word when spelled in English...

00:17:39.260 --> 00:17:41.380
the colors turn into numbers!

00:17:42.300 --> 00:17:44.220
That’s what you meant, 
isn’t it, Ana?

00:17:44.510 --> 00:17:45.240
Come again?

00:17:45.890 --> 00:17:47.720
In which case, this is...!

00:17:49.390 --> 00:17:50.720
A magic square!

00:17:50.720 --> 00:17:52.070
So I’ve gotta add the numbers across

00:17:52.070 --> 00:17:53.440
each column and row so they 
come to the same total,

00:17:53.440 --> 00:17:55.400
then plug those blocks into the puzzle.

00:17:55.400 --> 00:17:56.880
Let’s hurry, Gammon!

00:17:57.150 --> 00:17:57.910
Yeah!

00:17:59.900 --> 00:18:04.960
Impossible! Have they figured 
out my puzzle’s code?!

00:18:24.930 --> 00:18:26.260
Time’s up!

00:18:26.260 --> 00:18:29.220
You put up a good fight, but 
it’s been ten minutes!

00:18:30.700 --> 00:18:33.020
Gammon, we’re out of time!

00:18:33.020 --> 00:18:35.050
Not to worry!

00:18:35.770 --> 00:18:38.150
Throw that block over to me!

00:18:40.520 --> 00:18:42.300
Hurry!

00:18:44.570 --> 00:18:46.280
Gammon!

00:18:48.660 --> 00:18:50.520
Booyah!

00:18:54.790 --> 00:18:57.360
This is the last one!

00:19:12.510 --> 00:19:15.700
Im... Impossible!

00:19:17.060 --> 00:19:19.150
I won!

00:19:19.440 --> 00:19:24.640
Yay! Gammon won! Gammon won!

00:19:24.900 --> 00:19:27.890
Gammon won! Gammon won!

00:19:29.370 --> 00:19:34.460
He solved that difficult of a 
puzzle completely in his head?

00:19:34.830 --> 00:19:36.910
Impossible...!

00:19:36.910 --> 00:19:41.920
I can’t believe I lost 
to a mere $750,000 bounty.

00:19:42.750 --> 00:19:46.260
Gammon won! Gammon won!

00:19:47.090 --> 00:19:51.640
But I couldn’t have won by myself...!

00:19:53.970 --> 00:19:55.270
They did it!

00:19:56.600 --> 00:19:59.020
Whatcha think? We won!

00:20:00.100 --> 00:20:01.200
Indeed.

00:20:02.480 --> 00:20:03.350
But...!

00:20:05.190 --> 00:20:06.360
How terrifying...

00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:12.080
Maybe puzzles aren’t 
meant to exist after all.

00:20:13.370 --> 00:20:14.180
Jin...?

00:20:14.790 --> 00:20:16.690
See? I told you!

00:20:17.660 --> 00:20:19.450
Even without his memories,

00:20:19.450 --> 00:20:22.370
Jin’s hatred for puzzles 
hasn’t changed.

00:20:22.880 --> 00:20:23.780
Jin!

00:20:27.550 --> 00:20:31.140
However, it’s true 
that you won this round.

00:20:32.010 --> 00:20:34.470
Very well. I’ll let you keep Jin.

00:20:36.810 --> 00:20:39.230
Why don’t you work your butts off...

00:20:40.350 --> 00:20:41.720
to get Jin’s memories back?

00:20:52.870 --> 00:20:54.450
Is that right?

00:20:54.990 --> 00:20:58.910
Even in England, new assassins 
appeared under Jin’s name...

00:21:00.040 --> 00:21:06.170
The POG’s digital library also 
contained data warning about him.

00:21:07.170 --> 00:21:08.790
After thinking about it,

00:21:08.790 --> 00:21:11.680
I’ve realized I don’t 
know everything about Jin.

00:21:13.590 --> 00:21:15.250
Could you tell me?

00:21:15.720 --> 00:21:18.770
What happened in Jin’s past?

00:21:19.680 --> 00:21:21.900
In preparation for his fight 
with Count Pythagoras,

00:21:21.900 --> 00:21:23.900
Jin traveled across the world.

00:21:24.310 --> 00:21:25.480
During which time,

00:21:25.480 --> 00:21:27.480
he had a “blank year” that 
even I don’t know about.

00:21:28.650 --> 00:21:34.450
No one knows how exactly 
Jin spent that year.

00:21:45.790 --> 00:21:47.590
At last, it has begun!

00:21:48.380 --> 00:21:50.670
This is our battle.

00:21:58.310 --> 00:22:00.820
As the contract states, henceforth

00:22:00.820 --> 00:22:04.520
I would like you to do your 
utmost to defeat Kaito Daimon.

00:22:05.230 --> 00:22:07.630
This will also bring you closer 
to realizing Jin’s dream.

00:22:08.770 --> 00:22:11.220
I’m going to Root Gakuen.

00:22:12.490 --> 00:22:13.700
Why?!

00:22:13.700 --> 00:22:14.730
Because I want to.

00:22:20.040 --> 00:22:20.980
Goodness gracious.

00:22:22.750 --> 00:22:24.540
You’re such an unruly kitten.

00:24:04.470 --> 00:24:05.470
Look up to the sky!

00:24:05.470 --> 00:24:06.100
It’s a bird!

00:24:06.100 --> 00:24:07.100
It’s a plane!

00:24:07.100 --> 00:24:09.230
No, it’s a flying puzzle!

00:24:09.520 --> 00:24:12.570
You coward! Get down 
here so I can solve you!

00:24:12.570 --> 00:24:14.110
Ah, it really came down.

00:24:14.110 --> 00:24:14.860
What?!

00:24:14.860 --> 00:24:17.240
Takeda, please go solve it!

00:24:17.610 --> 00:24:19.990
Next time, “Even So, 
I Believe in Him.”

00:24:18.160 --> 00:24:27.970
Even So, I Believe in Him

00:24:20.110 --> 00:24:22.490
There's no puzzle I can't solve!

00:24:22.490 --> 00:24:26.190
Takeda! Takeda! Takeda, 
where are you going?!

00:24:27.970 --> 00:24:30.990
Fin Art: Akeru Otsuki
